.TH KINTSUGI-CONNECT 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-connect \- verify and store provider API keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi connect
\-\-list
.br
.B kintsugi connect
<provider> [\-\-no\-verify] [\-\-key\-stdin] [\-\-delete]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify and store provider API keys securely. Keys are stored with 0600
permissions in the credential store. Environment variables take precedence over
stored keys.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \fB\-\-list\fR
List configured providers and key status
.IP \fB\-\-no\-verify\fR
Save without pinging the provider first
.IP \fB\-\-key\-stdin\fR
Read the key from one line on stdin
.IP \fB\-\-delete\fR
Remove the stored key for the provider
.SH EXAMPLES
List all providers:
.PP
  $ kintsugi connect --list
.PP
Add a key interactively:
.PP
  $ kintsugi connect ollama
.PP
Add a key from stdin:
.PP
  $ echo "sk-..." | kintsugi connect openai --key-stdin
.PP
Skip verification:
.PP
  $ kintsugi connect custom-provider --no-verify
.PP
Remove a stored key:
.PP
  $ kintsugi connect ollama --delete
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-models (1)
